      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "No, even a superficial nick with a home-sterilized needle is unsafe because it cannot guarantee sterilization sufficient to prevent severe bacterial introduction. You are mistaken in thinking boiling water for 10 minutes is enough, as it does not kill spores and offers no protection against contaminants picked up during handling or skin brushing. Allowing fluid to escape unsanitarily simply creates a pathway for deeper infection, which can turn into a dangerous blood infection within hours or days. You must accept the temporary discomfort of professional care or use very simple home care like warm soaks, as the risk of serious harm is far greater than your potential minor inconvenience.",
